      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In this paper is used the rough set theory to deal with the information contained in electrocardiographic waveforms and to find out the correlation between coronary heart disease (CHD) and the selected indices in electrocardiographic lead I. The principles of attribute reduction are applied, the redundancy of a decision-making table is reduced, and the important characters and diagnostic rules are extracted. The real case analysis shows that clear and concise diagnostic rules can be established by using rough set theory, which can be helpful to the clinical diagnosis of CHD."},
